53777122498, 0.007254475262016058, 0.010155007243156433, -0.010217925533652306, 0.011130239814519882, 0.004479779861867428, -0.007015385664999485, -0.002235171152278781], "index": 15, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7606, "total_tokens": 7606}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP Technology Updates as of May 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and enhancements in SAP technology, focusing on components such as Pricing Service, SAP Build Process Automation, SAP HANA Service, Data Quality Services, and Mobile Services. The information highlights the importance of these updates in improving operational efficiency, user experience, and data management within the SAP ecosystem.\n\n## Pricing Service Enhancements\n\nThe Pricing Service has undergone several enhancements, including the ability to provide more data to requirement implementations, log inactivity due to missing routine implementations, and support for custom subtotal flags. These updates improve the accuracy and efficiency of pricing calculations, enabling businesses to make informed decisions. [Data: Sources (3001, 3002, 3004), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has introduced a new feature allowing users to connect and manage their events in one place, ensuring smooth execution and monitoring. This update enhances the overall user experience and improves event management within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (3007), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 02), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## SAP HANA Service Monitoring Enhancements\n\nThe SAP HANA Service has introduced a new metric to monitor unused memory in tenant databases, enabling users to optimize database performance and reduce costs. This update improves data management and operational efficiency within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (3008), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 02), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Data Quality Services Enhancements\n\nData Quality Services has introduced enhancements, including address validation in Bolivia, improved type-ahead suggestions for UK postcodes, and migration from the Neo environment to Cloud Foundry. These updates improve data accuracy and management within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (3009), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 05, 01))]\n\n## Mobile Services Updates\n\nMobile Services has introduced additional user interface languages, including Serbian (Cyrillic), Serbian (Latin), Montenegrin, and Macedonian. This update enhances the user experience and improves accessibility within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (3010), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 16), (2024, 05, 01))]", "# SAP Pricing Service and Related Components Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's Pricing Service and related components, highlighting their key features, updates, and integrations. The information is relevant to SAP's technology and business operations as of 2024.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates and Enhancements\n\nThe Pricing Service has undergone several updates and enhancements, including the addition of new features such as stateless pricing, support for custom subtotal flags, and integration with SAP Cloud ALM for performance monitoring. These updates aim to improve the service's efficiency and accuracy in pricing calculations. [Data: Sources (3001, 3002, 3003, 3004, 3005), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Integration with SAP Cloud ALM\n\nThe Pricing Service has been integrated with SAP Cloud ALM for performance monitoring and system monitoring. This integration enables real-time monitoring of pricing service calls and provides insights into system performance. [Data: Sources (3007, 3579, 3580), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 19), (2024, 01, 31))]\n\n## Support for Alternative Units of Measure\n\nThe Pricing Service now supports alternative units of measure, enabling SAP CPQ to work with condition rates that use different units. This feature enhances the service's flexibility and accuracy in pricing calculations. [Data: Source (3004), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime Updates as of May 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of recent updates to SAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime, highlighting key features and enhancements. The information is relevant to the development and maintenance of these platforms as of May 2025.\n\n## SAP Task Center API Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Task Center API has been updated to support direct authentication via SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Authentication. This enhancement enables users to access the API more securely and efficiently. The update is part of the SAP Cloud Foundry platform and is available as of May 7, 2025 [Data: Sources (518, 519), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 07))].\n\n## New Commercial Plan for SAP Task Center\n\nA new service plan, build-default, has been made available for SAP Task Center. This plan provides users with more flexibility and control over their application development and deployment. The update is part of the SAP Cloud Foundry platform and is available as of May 7, 2025 [Data: Sources (518, 519), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 07))].\n\n## Variant Configuration API Enhancements\n\nThe Variant Configuration API has been updated to support several new features, including the ability to return context and source when creating a new configuration, and the ability to lock configurations against changes. These enhancements improve the usability and security of the API. The update is part of the SAP Cloud Foundry platform and is available as of May 7, 2025 [Data: Sources (953, 954), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 15), (2025, 05, 07))].\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has been updated to include several new features and enhancements, including an updated Istio version. These updates improve the performance and security of the platform. The update is available as of May 2025 [Data: Sources (958), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 07))].", "# SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's Variant Configuration and Pricing key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide configuration and pricing solutions effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Variant Configuration Operational Scope\n\nThe Variant Configuration Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating configuration risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential configuration pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective configuration management not only prevents configuration anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (738, 813), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 15), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Knowledge Bases API and Search Functionality\n\nThe Knowledge Bases API at SAP enables the search for knowledge bases by the BOM application, for example SD01 or PP01. This new filter value called bomApplication for endpoint GET /kbdetermination is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (814, 956), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 15), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Configuration\n\nCollaboration between the Variant Configuration and Pricing components, established in Q2 2025, ensures that configuration mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (815, 957), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 15), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP Technology and Pricing Service Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and pricing services, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (596, 597, 598, 599, 600), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Technology and Pricing Service Integration\n\nThe integration of the Pricing Service and Technology Departments at SAP ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (596, 597, 598, 599, 600), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry and Pricing Service Enhancements\n\nThe enhancements to the Pricing Service in Cloud Foundry, such as the introduction of new endpoints for currency conversion and condition determination, demonstrate the company's commitment to improving its pricing capabilities. These enhancements support the company's strategic decision-making processes and ensure continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (596, 597, 598, 599, 600), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Data Attribute Recommendation Improvements\n\nThe improvements to the Data Attribute Recommendation service, such as calibration enhancements and data validation improvements, demonstrate the company's commitment to improving its data management capabilities. These enhancements support the company's strategic decision-making processes and ensure continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (942, 943, 944), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 07))]\n\n## Cloud Integration for Data Services Enhancements\n\nThe enhancements to the Cloud Integration for Data Services, such as the addition of new features and improvements to existing ones, demonstrate the company's commitment to improving its data management capabilities. These enhancements support the company's strategic decision-making processes and ensure continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (941), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 07))]", "# Cloud Integration and Data Services Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key components and services within the cloud integration and data services framework, highlighting their relationships and core attributes. The information is relevant to the company's operations around May 2025.\n\n## Cloud Integration for Data Services Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Integration for Data Services component plays a pivotal role in facilitating data exchange and integration across various systems. Its proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard the company against potential data inconsistencies and ensures continuous compliance with evolving data standards. Effective cloud integration not only prevents data anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (87, 88), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 07))]\n\n## Data Attribute Recommendation Improvements\n\nThe Data Attribute Recommendation component has undergone significant improvements, including enhanced calibration of classification models. The returned probabilities are now more robust and reliable, ensuring accurate data recommendations. This improvement underscores the commitment to upholding high data standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (1466), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 06), (2025, 05, 07))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Data Services\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Integration for Data Services and Data Attribute Recommendation components ensures that data exchange and integration strategies are effective and reliable. This synergy is vital for holistic data governance and has been instrumental in integrating data services with cloud integration strategies at the company. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with data standards. [Data: Sources (87, 1466), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 07))]", "# SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on variant configuration and pricing, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide effective pricing solutions. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP plays a pivotal role in providing pricing solutions. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential pricing pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective pricing management not only prevents pricing anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (596, 801, 805), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Variant Configuration and Pricing Integration\n\nThe Variant Configuration and Pricing departments at SAP ensure that all pricing solutions adhere to the configuration standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on integration and collaboration, noted starting mid-2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex pricing configurations and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high configuration standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (738, 813, 817), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 15), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Pricing\n\nCollaboration between the Pricing Service and Variant Configuration departments, established in mid-2025, ensures that pricing solutions are configuration-compliant and that configuration measures consider pricing risks. This synergy is vital for holistic pricing governance and has been instrumental in integrating pricing with configuration strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9, 817), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 15), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024-10-02\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations as of 2024-10-02.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP Cloud Services has undergone several updates, including the addition of new endpoints and enhancements to existing ones. These changes aim to improve the service's functionality and user experience. For example, the new endpoint for returning condition rates in document currency for group conditions has been added to address a previous issue. [Data: Sources (596, 803), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 01), (2024, 10, 02))]\n\n## SAP Task Center Enhancements\n\nSAP Task Center has received several enhancements, including improved notification display and substitution management for business administrators. These updates aim to improve the user experience and increase operational efficiency. For example, notifications are now displayed consistently for all supported task providers without being deleted every 24 hours. [Data: Sources (807, 2187), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 01), (2024, 10, 02))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Upgrade\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, providing improved functionality and security. This upgrade is part of the company's efforts to maintain a secure and efficient technological infrastructure. [Data: Source (2183), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 10, 02))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of May 2025. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone several updates as of May 2025, including the introduction of new endpoints and enhancements to existing ones. These updates aim to improve the service's functionality and user experience. For example, the new endpoint GET /currencyConversion/currencies allows users to read settings of currency codes, while the enhancement of stateless pricing and document pricing endpoints provides more detailed pricing results. [Data: Sources (596, 802, 803, 804), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 16), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP have also seen significant updates as of May 2025. These updates include the introduction of new features, such as password management and regular upgrades, as well as enhancements to existing features, such as SAML 2.0 configuration. These updates aim to improve the security and functionality of Cloud Identity Services. [Data: Sources (791, 792, 793, 794), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 21), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Technology\n\nCollaboration between SAP's technology components, such as Pricing Service and Cloud Identity Services, is essential for ensuring that technology strategies are aligned with business requirements. As of May 2025, these components have been working together to provide seamless and efficient technology services. [Data: Sources (596, 791), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 16), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their operational scope, core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations around May 2025.\n\n## Feature Flags Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Feature Flags Service at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in enabling the sharing of SAP Feature Flags service instances between different Cloud Foundry organizations in the same subaccount. This feature is applicable when using feature flags and configurations of a single service instance in two SAP BTP landscapes - a main and an extension one. The service instance sharing capability is essential for efficient feature management and deployment across multiple environments. [Data: Sources (877), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime at SAP BTP has undergone updates, including the API Gateway module, which has been updated to version 3.0.3. This update brings improvements such as fixing the extAuth handler not being scoped to a particular host and reconciliation of convertible APIRules. The update also addresses the issue of the original-version annotation not being set if it's already present in the APIRule. These improvements enhance the overall performance and reliability of the Kyma Runtime. [Data: Sources (878), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP BTP have been enhanced with features such as password management, regular upgrades, and SAML 2.0 configuration. The password management feature allows users to configure the system to show a password expiration reminder at the sign-in page. The regular upgrades ensure that the services are always up-to-date and secure. The SAML 2.0 configuration feature has been updated to include an Entity ID field. These enhancements improve the overall security and usability of Cloud Identity Services. [Data: Sources (791, 792, 793, 794), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 21), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# Cloud Identity Services and Integration Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key components and services within the Cloud Identity Services and Integration framework, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to the company's operations and strategic planning.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has undergone significant updates as of 2025, including the introduction of new features such as password management, regular upgrades, and support for externalId in UUID format. These updates aim to enhance the overall user experience and improve the security of the system. [Data: Sources (17, 18, 19, 20, 21), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 21), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Integration Advisor Updates\n\nThe Integration Advisor has also seen updates, including the introduction of overlay mapping guidelines, which allow users to customize and extend base mapping guidelines. This feature aims to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of integration processes. [Data: Sources (1250), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 11), (2025, 03, 11))]\n\n## Forms Service by Adobe Updates\n\nThe Forms Service by Adobe has introduced new output types, including CAB, DPL, IPL, PCL, PS, TPCL, and ZPL. This update aims to enhance the flexibility and versatility of the service. [Data: Sources (1311), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 27))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of January 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key components and their relationships, highlighting the importance of these entities in maintaining the platform's stability and security. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of January 2024.\n\n## Risk Management and Security Measures\n\nSAP BTP has implemented various risk management and security measures to protect the platform from potential threats. The hardening of security standards on client certificates and their certificate chains, announced in May 2023 and implemented in November 2023, is a significant step towards enhancing platform security. This change will result in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform, ensuring that only secure connections are allowed. The implementation of this change is scheduled to be completed by February 22, 2024. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2023, 05, 01), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP BTP's components, such as Risk Management and Legal Compliance, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2024, 01, 26))]\n\n## New Features and Enhancements\n\nSAP BTP has introduced several new features and enhancements to improve the platform's functionality and user experience. The addition of new components, such as the SAP Build Process Automation and the SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition, has expanded the platform's capabilities and provided users with more options for customization and integration. The implementation of these new features and enhancements is ongoing, with the latest updates being released in January 2024. [Data: Sources (3613, 3614, 3615, 3616, 3617, 3618, 3619), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 01, 26))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of January 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key components and their relationships, highlighting their roles in ensuring the platform's security, compliance, and operational efficiency. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's technology landscape around January 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Security Enhancements\n\nSAP BTP has implemented several security enhancements to strengthen its platform security. One notable enhancement is the hardening of security standards on certain properties for client certificates and their certificate chains, which will result in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform. This change is scheduled to be rolled out on February 22, 2024. [Data: Sources (2), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP BTP's various components, such as Risk Management and Legal Compliance, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## New Features and Updates\n\nSAP BTP has introduced several new features and updates to enhance its platform's functionality and user experience. These include the ability to manage API credentials for calling REST APIs of the SAP Authorization and Trust Management service, the introduction of Kubernetes operators, and the provision of global account and directory members using the SCIM API. These updates underscore the commitment to upholding high standards of security, compliance, and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 11), (2024, 01, 25))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Related Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and related services, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold platform security and manage services effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Deprecation of Weak Client Certificate Chains\n\nThe SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime has announced the deprecation of weak client certificate chains, which will be removed in early 2024 to further strengthen platform security. This change will result in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform. The remaining regions are scheduled to follow on February 22, 2024. Note that this change only affects client certificates. If you do not use client certificates/mTLS to authenticate with the platform, you are not affected. [Data: Sources (3952, 3602), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Removal of .NET, Ruby, and R Buildpacks\n\nThe .NET, Ruby, and R offline buildpacks have been deprecated and are scheduled to be removed from the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment on November 16, 2023. If you want to continue using these buildpacks after their removal, you can use the online community buildpacks by specifying their URLs in the code of your applications. [Data: Source (3951), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 16))]\n\n## Additional NAT and LB IPs Added to Amazon Web Services Regions\n\nAdditional NAT and Load Balancer (LB) IP addresses were added on SAP BTP regions running on Amazon Web Services (AWS). The following regions are affected by this change: br10 – Brazil (São Paulo), jp10 – Japan (Tokyo), ap10 – Australia (Sydney), ap11 – Asia Pacific (Singapore), ap12 – Asia Pacific (Seoul), ca10 – Canada (Montreal), eu10 – Europe (Frankfurt), eu11 – Europe (Frankfurt), us10 – US East (VA). [Data: Source (3953), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 01, Q1))]\n\n## SAP BTP Service Operator - Fixed SAP Kubernetes Service Binding Specification\n\nThe Secret created for the service binding contains an instance name key in the service instance info section. This key uses the BTP name of the service binding, which is the value of the external_name property in the service binding spec. The external_instance_name key has been removed from the secret. [Data: Source (3954), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 11), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 8\n\nJava Web Tomcat 8 (runtime version 3.190) has been updated to Tomcat version 8.5.95. The new version contains security fixes. See the Changelog. Recommended action: Update your applications to the latest runtime version. [Data: Source (3955), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Limits for Roles, Role Collections, Trust, and Service Broker Instances\n\nThere are limits that apply when you define roles, role collections, trust, and service broker instances. [Data: Source (3956), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Backend\n\nEnabled Visual cloud functions user authorization feature. Visual cloud functions are now available for consumption from applications deployed to SAP Build Workzone. [Data: Source (3601), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 01, 26))]\n\n## New Quick Action for Global Account Administrators to Assign Themselves as Subaccount Administrators in the Account Explorer\n\nIf you're a global account administrator, you can now easily assign yourself as an administrator of any subaccount in your account structure. Go to the Account Explorer page in the SAP BTP cockpit and look for the new Add Me as Admin option in the  (Actions) context menu of the listed subaccounts. [Data: Source (3603), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 11), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Management of API Credentials for Calling REST APIs of SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service\n\nWe’ve added a new way to manage technical credentials for REST APIs of the SAP Authorization and Trust Management service. It's no longer restricted to multi-environment subaccounts with a Cloud Foundry environment, but works independently from environments in any multi-environment subaccount, directory, and global account. Most importantly, you can now also provision global account and directory members using the SCIM API. [Data: Source (3604), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 11), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Kubernetes Operators\n\nSAP Automation Pilot is set to offer you an opportunity to create and execute Kubernetes operators, capitalizing on the same user-friendly low-code/no-code tools already available in the service for alternate environments. [Data: Source (3605), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Remote Work Processor\n\nSAP Automation Pilot defined an additional permission called Remote Work Processor which allows you to create run configuration entities when managing Kubernetes operators. The permission helps to establish a successful connection between a remote work processor deployed on a customer environment and the SAP Automation Pilot backend. [Data: Source (3606), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 01, 25))]", "# SAP BTP and Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key cloud services focusing on BTP and related entities, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a robust and secure cloud platform. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Security Enhancements\n\nSAP BTP has been enhancing its security standards by deprecating weak client certificate chains and raising the OpenSSL security level to 2. This change has been rolled out in various regions, with the remaining regions scheduled to follow in February 2024. Effective security management not only prevents potential security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3952, 3957), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Cloud Connector and IP Addresses\n\nThe Cloud Connector has been updated with additional IP addresses for various SAP BTP regions running on Amazon Web Services (AWS). This change affects regions such as br10, jp10, ap10, and others. It is essential for users to update their firewall rules to allow access to these new IP addresses, which will be used after March 31, 2024. [Data: Sources (3383, 3384), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 16), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## SAP BTP Region Updates\n\nSAP BTP regions have been updated with additional NAT and LB IP addresses for various regions, including br10, jp10, ap10, and others. This change affects users who restrict system access by allowlisting IPs in firewall rules. It is essential to update the configuration as soon as possible to avoid any disruptions. [Data: Sources (3953, 3384), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 02, 22))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's cloud services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud infrastructure and services as of 2023.\n\n## SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\n\nSAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration is a key component of SAP's cloud services, enabling seamless integration with external credit agencies. The recent integration with Rubix Data Sciences highlights the company's commitment to expanding its credit integration capabilities. This integration is crucial for supporting SAP's financial services and risk management efforts. [Data: Sources (526), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 30), (2023, 11, 30))]\n\n## Deprecation of Weak Client Certificate Chains\n\nThe deprecation of weak client certificate chains in SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime, is a significant update to SAP's cloud security standards. This change aims to harden security and prevent potential vulnerabilities. The update is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to enhance its cloud infrastructure and protect customer data. [Data: Sources (2), Date_Range ((2023, 05, 18), (2023, 11, 29))]\n\n## Kyma Dashboard Updates\n\nThe recent update to the Kyma dashboard, featuring a new look and modern design, is a significant improvement to SAP's cloud services. The update aims to enhance user experience and provide a more intuitive interface for managing cloud services. This change is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to improve its cloud infrastructure and support customer needs. [Data: Sources (3), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 27), (2023, 11, 29))]\n\n## Identity Authentication Updates\n\nThe recent updates to Identity Authentication, including regional availability and regular upgrades, highlight SAP's commitment to enhancing its cloud identity services. The updates aim to provide a more secure and reliable identity management experience for customers. This change is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to improve its cloud infrastructure and support customer needs. [Data: Sources (6, 7, 8), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 27), (2023, 11, 28))]\n\n## Manage Transformations History\n\nThe recent update to Identity Provisioning, enabling the management of transformations history, is a significant improvement to SAP's cloud services. The update aims to provide customers with greater control over their transformation history and support more efficient management of their cloud infrastructure. This change is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to improve its cloud infrastructure and support customer needs. [Data: Sources (9, 10), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 27), (2023, 12, 06))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_1b6b6e1c0050eb8336a26b331a15239bfa4c822729ce343b3254f5b63f8e8668_v2"}